**For all examples im using this function wraaper**
```JS
function selAll(selector) {
	return document.querySelectorAll(selector)
}

function sel(selector) {
	return document.querySelector(selector)
}
const nodes = selAll(.box);
```

```JS
const node = sel("#first");
node.style.backgroundColor("green");

node.className = "box";
node.className = "orange";
// <div id=first class="box"> -> <div id=first class="orange">
node.classList.add("blue");
// <div id=first class="orange"> -> <div id=first class="orange blue">
```

It's comment to hide and show elements
```CSS
.hide {display : none}
.show {display : block}
```
So you can toggle like this
```js
node.classList.toggle("hide");
```
To modify structure you can do this
```js
const n2 = document.createElement("p");
// Creates an element in memory

n2.textContent = "Hello"

node.appendChild(n2)
// Adds element to the document which will change what the browser is displaying.
```

Setting attributes
```JS
img.setAttribute("src", "abc.gif");
img.setAttribute("alt", "stuff");
```
